Review fix (T8, test_review_relocate.py): relocate() served a moved claim as current.

The same-position hash check ran first, so when identical text landed at the anchor's old line inside another
function (a function inserted above), the anchor read as 'unchanged' while pointing into the wrong function.
Now the same-position match counts only when the enclosing symbol is still the anchor's symbol (or that symbol
no longer exists); otherwise the search below finds it, narrowed to its own symbol.

Apply from the repo root: git apply docs/patches/review-relocate.patch

--- a/src/honeyguide/anchors.py
